# tests/oracle.rs hashes scenes/*.toml byte for byte, and Windows checks text files
# out as CRLF by default, so a Windows clone changes those bytes and fails
# scene_sha256 while rendering pixel-identical output. Pinning the working tree to LF
# everywhere keeps one hash true on every platform. The goldens under tests/goldens/
# are detected as binary by text=auto and are left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
